From c2f066a6d0982f2476cdd5bef8b53ba10fa7eef9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:18:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: comments record writer_kind (agent/human);
 live notes say when an agent wrote them

The kanban_comment tool is always an agent, but nothing recorded it. David and his agents share one
profile, so a chat agent's note reached the worker stamped 'default (another session)' under
'from the operator', and the ask-gate scored 'Please re-check (c) yourself' as David (agent-261aa31f49).

- add_comment(writer_kind='agent'|'human', writer_session=...) stores them on the commented event
  (additive; unset for system writers and legacy callers; other values raise).
- kanban_comment tool: agent + request-scoped session id. CLI / slash command and dashboard (Desktop): human.
- inject_new_comments_from_env stamps agent lines '(agent chat, another session)'; when every line is an
  agent's, the header is 'from another agent session'.

Proof: tests/tools/test_kanban_comment_writer_kind.py 7 red -> green; 59 comment-touching test files
1146 passed.
